# Offline cell-tower database for rhodep-gnss-daemon's `cell` source.
#
# Read by rhodep-cell-db.service, which is driven by rhodep-cell-db.timer.
# NEITHER IS ENABLED BY DEFAULT, on purpose: a refresh streams the full
# OpenCelliD dump, which is 1.1 GB, and a package should not decide on your
# behalf to pull that over what may be a metered link. Turn it on with
#
#     systemctl enable --now rhodep-cell-db.timer
#
# or just build the database once, by hand:
#
#     rhodep-cell-db build --mcc 722 --source ocid,mls
#
# Neither is required. Without a database the cell source simply starts at the
# network providers instead, which is where it would end up anyway for any cell
# the dumps do not have.

# Mobile country codes to index, comma-separated. 722 is Argentina.
# Each extra country costs disk and download time but nothing at query time.
# See https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mobile_country_code
MCC="722"

# Which dumps to merge, in order of preference; the first one named wins where
# they disagree about a cell.
#   ocid  Internet Archive mirror of the OpenCelliD full export, 2024-05-19,
#         CC-BY-SA 4.0. 1.1 GB compressed.
#   mls   Internet Archive copy of the final Mozilla Location Service cell
#         export, 2024-03-27, public domain. 1.6 GB compressed. Frozen for
#         good -- MLS shut down in 2024 -- but it was an independent survey,
#         so it has cells OpenCelliD does not. MEASURED for MCC 722: ocid
#         alone gives 312k cells, ocid+mls gives 653k.
# You can also give a URL or a local .csv/.csv.gz here.
SOURCE="ocid,mls"

# Where to write it. The daemon's --cell-db default is this same path.
DB="/var/lib/rhodep-gnss/cells.sqlite"

# If you have an OpenCelliD API access token, put it here and the official
# per-MCC export is downloaded instead of the mirror: far smaller, and current
# rather than two years old. Tokens are free but registration is a web form
# with a reCAPTCHA, so there is no way to obtain one from a script and this
# package does not ship one. https://opencellid.org/
#TOKEN=""
